below the 1990s=E2=80=99 peak of over 10%:=0A=0AWeisberger points out that =
while that appears massive, it=E2=80=99s highly =0Aconcentrated, largely th=
anks to SpaceX. Only about 200 companies came to market =0Aover the past 12=
 months, roughly one-third of previous peaks.=0A=0AThis raises questions ab=
out how equities can absorb the additional supply. In =0Athispaper =0A<http=
s://www.gmo.com/americas/research-library/a-catalyst-for-the-ai-bubble-brea=
